            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Derek Howard",
                        "email": "derekh@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "derekhoward55"
                    },
                    "message": "Looks great!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "This isn't true today, are you going to change it across all current systems?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "I had planned to.  It would make the code simpler to write, and I think it matches the idea that chassis0 is the whole system and not the first chassis.\n\nI realize this means this documentation doesn't match the current code.  I'll be submitting commits in the future that implement this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 176,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "In the previous sections you listed some examples of how the property could be set to false, could you do that here? I think a lot of people are probably a bit overwhelmed by the number of properties we look at so the examples really help understand the use cases."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 176,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "The sub-sections on brownout and blackout go into more detail on what causes this to be Faulted.  But I can add more here too."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 176,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 185,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "is this the new one?  since there's lots of different places that refer to these apps that all have simliar names maybe in a high level spot you could just list all of the involved apps and a sentence or two of detail.  (or maybe i just missed it or haven't reviewed it yet)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 185,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, this is the new app.  Good suggestion I'll add something for this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 185,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Done.  Added list of related apps to the README.md file."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 221,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "are you already doing this in the polling that goes on?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 221,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes.  I was just trying to explain for each chassis status property whether we can read the chassis pgood and what the corresponding pgood property will be set to.  For example, when Present is false, we can't read chassis pgood, and we will set the pgood property to false."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 221,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 222,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "This one is a bit surprising to me, that we actually try and power on during a brownout? I'm not sure the PSM code will allow a power on if it sees an active brownout condition."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 222,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "I discussed this with my team lead, and he agrees with you.  This design had been intended to cover some corner cases.  But we can instead *not* power the drawer on and log an error so the customer knows why it wasn't powered on."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/docs/chassis_status.md",
                    "line": 222,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Done."
                }
            ],
